refsection.programlisting:
F = gf_create_field(2, 4); // 1 + x + x^4 gf_minimal_polynomial(F, 1) // [1 1 0 0 1]: alpha has the field's polynomial gf_minimal_polynomial(F, 3) // [1 1 1 1 1] gf_minimal_polynomial(F, 5) // [1 1 1 0 0]: alpha^5 lies in the subfield GF(4) gf_minimal_polynomial(F, 0) // [1 1 0 0 0]: 1 + x for the element 1 gf_minimal_polynomial(F, -1) // [0 1 0 0 0]: x for the element 0
// Element given by its coefficients k = gf_to_exponential(F, [1 1 0 1]); gf_minimal_polynomial(F, k)
// Without creating the field first gf_minimal_polynomial(7, 1, 3) // [4 1]: x - 3
